{"type":"message","id":"3ef80754","parentId":"b1b95d12","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:16:44.895Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8da0c8a092da3e44","name":"edit","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/coinography-run-20260728-120854-96194-23933/article/raw.md","edits":[{"oldText":"# Bitkub Hid $53M Theft From Regulators For Five Months","newText":"# Bitkub Theft: Exchange Hid $53M From Thai SEC"},{"oldText":"Thailand's Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint against [Bitkub](https://cryptoslate.com/how-a-crypto-exchange-secretly-hid-53m-in-stolen-crypto-to-prevent-a-bank-run-and-why-the-sec-is-finally-coming-for-its-directors/), the country's largest cryptocurrency exchange, for concealing a theft of roughly 1.7 billion baht, approximately $53 million, from regulators for nearly six months.","newText":"Thailand's Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint over a Bitkub theft of roughly 1.7 billion baht, approximately $53 million, that the country's largest cryptocurrency exchange allegedly concealed from regulators for nearly six months."},{"oldText":"- Primary Keyword: Bitkub theft","newText":"- Primary Keyword: Bitkub $53M theft"},{"oldText":"- Meta Description: Thai SEC files criminal complaint against Bitkub for concealing a $53 million theft in daily reports, alleging false filings after a 2021 hack.","newText":"- Meta Description: Thai SEC files criminal complaint over Bitkub $53M theft concealed in daily reports, alleging false filings after a 2021 hack."},{"oldText":"- URL Slug: bitkub-53m-theft-thai-sec-complaint","newText":"- URL Slug: bitkub-53m-theft-thai-sec"},{"oldText":"- SEO Title: Bitkub Hid $53M Theft: Thai SEC Files Criminal Complaint","newText":"- SEO Title: Bitkub $53M Theft: Thai SEC Files Criminal Complaint"},{"oldText":"[Word Count: 1112]","newText":"[Word Count: 1113]"}]}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"bedrock-mantle","model":"zai.glm-5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1785240994912,"responseId":"chatcmpl-47bf80d8-3f2d-4104-8fcf-ebb17cb8754b"}}
{"type":"message","id":"c947f2c7","parentId":"3ef80754","timestamp":"2026-07-28T12:16:45.255Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-8da0c8a092da3e44","toolName":"edit","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully replaced 7 block(s) in /tmp/coinography-run-20260728-120854-96194-23933/article/raw.md."}],"details":{"diff":"  1 META\n- 2 - SEO Title: Bitkub Hid $53M Theft: Thai SEC Files Criminal Complaint\n- 3 - Meta Description: Thai SEC files criminal complaint against Bitkub for concealing a $53 million theft in daily reports, alleging false filings after a 2021 hack.\n- 4 - URL Slug: bitkub-53m-theft-thai-sec-complaint\n+ 2 - SEO Title: Bitkub $53M Theft: Thai SEC Files Criminal Complaint\n+ 3 - Meta Description: Thai SEC files criminal complaint over Bitkub $53M theft concealed in daily reports, alleging false filings after a 2021 hack.\n+ 4 - URL Slug: bitkub-53m-theft-thai-sec\n  5 - Categories: Exploits News, SEC\n- 6 - Primary Keyword: Bitkub theft\n+ 6 - Primary Keyword: Bitkub $53M theft\n  7 - Secondary Keywords: Thai SEC, crypto exchange hack, $53 million stolen, bank run prevention\n  8 \n  9 ---\n 10 \n-11 # Bitkub Hid $53M Theft From Regulators For Five Months\n+11 # Bitkub Theft: Exchange Hid $53M From Thai SEC\n 12 \n-13 Thailand's Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint against [Bitkub](https://cryptoslate.com/how-a-crypto-exchange-secretly-hid-53m-in-stolen-crypto-to-prevent-a-bank-run-and-why-the-sec-is-finally-coming-for-its-directors/), the country's largest cryptocurrency exchange, for concealing a theft of roughly 1.7 billion baht, approximately $53 million, from regulators for nearly six months. The July 23, 2026 complaint alleges that Bitkub submitted false daily net-capital reports that failed to reflect the impact of a May 2021 cyberattack, while two former directors oversaw the cover-up.\n+13 Thailand's Securities and Exchange Commission has filed a criminal complaint over a Bitkub theft of roughly 1.7 billion baht, approximately $53 million, that the country's largest cryptocurrency exchange allegedly concealed from regulators for nearly six months. The July 23, 2026 complaint alleges that Bitkub submitted false daily net-capital reports that failed to reflect the impact of a May 2021 cyberattack, while two former directors oversaw the cover-up.\n 14 \n 15 ## The $53 Million Hack And Cover-up\n 16 \n 17 The Thai SEC's complaint centers on events that began in May 2021, when hackers stole customer assets across 16 cryptocurrencies from the exchange. Rather than reporting the incident, Bitkub allegedly filed daily Form DA 1 reports from May 10 through October 30, 2021, showing no material change in its asset balance despite the massive theft.\n    ...\n 81 **Sources:**\n 82 - CryptoSlate: https://cryptoslate.com/how-a-crypto-exchange-secretly-hid-53m-in-stolen-crypto-to-prevent-a-bank-run-and-why-the-sec-is-finally-coming-for-its-directors/\n 83 - Bitcoin Foundation: https://bitcoinfoundation.org/news/crypto-companies-news/thai-sec-accuses-bitkub-of-concealing-51-million-hack/\n 84 \n-85 [Word Count: 1112]\n+85 [Word Count: 1113]","firstChangedLine":2},"isError":false,"timestamp":1785241005254}}
